# AWS CLI and System Stress Testing on Ubuntu 24.04

## 1. Install AWS CLI on Ubuntu 24.04

Update packages:

```bash
sudo apt update
```

Install required packages:

```bash
sudo apt install unzip curl -y
```

Download AWS CLI v2:

```bash
curl "https://awscli.amazonaws.com/awscli-exe-linux-x86_64.zip" -o "awscliv2.zip"
```

Extract the installer:

```bash
unzip -q awscliv2.zip
```

Install AWS CLI:

```bash
sudo ./aws/install
```

Check the installation:

```bash
aws --version
```

Check AWS CLI help:

```bash
aws help
```

---

## 2. Stress Test for CPU Load

Install the stress package:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install stress -y
```

Generate CPU load using all available CPU cores:

```bash
stress --cpu $(nproc) --timeout 600
```

The command will generate CPU load for **600 seconds (10 minutes)**.

---

## 3. Continuous System Load Monitoring

Install monitoring and stress-testing tools:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y stress-ng sysstat iotop iftop
```

Check the `stress-ng` version:

```bash
stress-ng --version
```

Start continuous system load:

```bash
nohup stress-ng --cpu 0 --cpu-load 70 --vm 0 --vm-bytes 60% --io 2 --hdd 2 --hdd-bytes 1G --timeout 0 > /tmp/stress-ng.out 2>&1 & echo $! > /tmp/stress.pid
```

> `--timeout 0` means the stress test will continue until it is manually stopped.

---

## 4. Monitor System Resources

Use `top` to monitor CPU and memory:

```bash
top
```

Other useful commands:

```bash
free -h
```

```bash
iostat
```

```bash
iotop
```

```bash
iftop
```

---

## 5. Stop the Continuous Stress Test

The process ID is stored in:

```bash
cat /tmp/stress.pid
```

Stop the stress process:

```bash
kill $(cat /tmp/stress.pid)
```

If required, force stop:

```bash
kill -9 $(cat /tmp/stress.pid)
```

Verify that the stress process has stopped:

```bash
ps aux | grep stress-ng
```

## Important

Do not leave continuous stress testing running unnecessarily because it consumes CPU, memory, disk I/O, and may increase EC2 usage/cost.

For AWS monitoring practicals, start the stress test only when you need to observe CloudWatch metrics.
